# CloudNativePG governance repository CODEOWNERS.
#
# See GOVERNANCE.md and subprojects/README.md for what these teams are and
# how they roll out. Team slugs referenced here without full repo access
# yet fall back to @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners, this repo's own
# owners team, the same transitional rule described in
# subprojects/README.md's GitHub Teams table.

# Default owners for everything not matched more specifically below.
* @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners

# GOVERNANCE.md, MAINTAINERS.md, and CONTRIBUTOR_LADDER.md are Steering
# Committee-owned documents (see GOVERNANCE.md's Voting section);
# ownership here is expressed through governance-owners, this repo's own
# owners team, same as the default rule above.
/GOVERNANCE.md @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/MAINTAINERS.md @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/CONTRIBUTOR_LADDER.md @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners

# Each subproject's own component listing is scoped to that subproject's
# maintainer committee team. All four teams exist and match MAINTAINERS.md,
# and all four hold write here (cnpg-infra's repo-policy.yaml), without
# which GitHub would ignore these lines entirely. `governance-owners` is
# listed alongside each while every committee still holds the same five
# people. The subprojects index itself stays on the `governance-owners`
# rule alone, since it isn't owned by any single subproject.
/subprojects/README.md @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/subprojects/core.md @cloudnative-pg/core-maintainers @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/subprojects/supply-chain.md @cloudnative-pg/supply-chain-maintainers @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/subprojects/community-ecosystem.md @cloudnative-pg/community-ecosystem-maintainers @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
/subprojects/extensibility.md @cloudnative-pg/extensibility-maintainers @cloudnative-pg/governance-owners
